# Gitignored files Claude Code copies into every worktree it creates with git
# (`claude --worktree`, subagent worktrees, background sessions). Only a path
# that is also gitignored is copied; tests/test_check_handoff_landing.py pins that.
#
# Claude Code reads the shared .claude/settings.json from the session's primary
# working directory, and a worktree checks out tracked files only. Without this
# line a session launched in a worktree loads none of the harness's hooks: no
# banner, no guards, no stop gate (measured 2026-10-08). A worktree created
# before this file existed needs the copy by hand; the landing check names it.
.claude/settings.json

# The codename gate's local pattern file: absent in a worktree, the gate runs on
# its tracked list alone (the landing check's local arm says so).
.local-codenames.txt
